  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of the rules! The most common way to lose is forgetting a rule that was made four rounds ago. In the early game, get rid of your high-point cards (Face cards).\n\nRule Synergies: If there's a rule that says 'The next player draws 2 on a 7', and you hold two 7s, try to hold them until the player to your left is low on cards.\n\nRule Manipulation: When you win, create a rule that targets a specific card you know is gone from the deck or one that you personally have many of in the next hand (if you can predict the shuffle). Or, create a rule that is linguistically difficult ('Must speak only in rhymes on Clubs').",
    Player: "Keep track of the rules! The most common way to lose is forgetting a rule that was made four rounds ago. In the early game, get rid of your high-point cards (Face cards).\n\nRule Synergies: If there's a rule that says 'The next player draws 2 on a 7', and you hold two 7s, try to hold them until the player to your left is low on cards.\n\nRule Manipulation: When you win, create a rule that targets a specific card you know is gone from the deck or one that you personally have many of in the next hand (if you can predict the shuffle). Or, create a rule that is linguistically difficult ('Must speak only in rhymes on Clubs').",
